# Response headers in Cloudflare Pages / Netlify `_headers` format.
# Other hosts: set the same name/value pairs in server or platform config.
# Rules: SEC-02, SEC-03, SEC-04 (CSP), PRF-17 (caching).
# CSP starts as Report-Only. When the console shows no violations, rename it to Content-Security-Policy.
# Each inline script (consent default and GTM loader) needs its own hash: script-src 'self' 'sha256-…'.
# The GTM/GA4 origins below cover GA4 only; Ads and Google signals need more (Google's CSP guide for Tag Manager). Remove them if no Google tags are used.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://www.googletagmanager.com; img-src 'self' data: https://www.googletagmanager.com https://*.google-analytics.com; connect-src 'self' https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com https://www.googletagmanager.com; style-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests

# Fingerprinted build output: cache for a year. Match your build tool's folder (e.g. /_astro/*, /_next/static/*).
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/.well-known/security.txt
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
